legal.privacyS3Body:
We process Personal Data for the following purposes, as applicable:

• To provide, operate, maintain, and improve the Service, including synchronization across devices where offered;
• To create and manage your account, authenticate you, and enforce access controls;
• To process transactions, fulfill subscriptions, communicate billing changes, and provide customer support;
• To secure the Service, detect, prevent, and respond to fraud, abuse, security incidents, and technical issues;
• To comply with applicable law, regulation, legal process, or governmental requests, and to enforce our Terms and other policies;
• To communicate with you regarding service-related notices (including security and administrative messages) and, where permitted, optional newsletters or digests you have not opted out of;
• To analyze aggregated or de-identified usage in a manner that does not reasonably identify you, where permitted.

If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, we describe our legal bases below at a high level. The appropriate basis depends on the specific processing activity:

• Contract: processing necessary to perform our agreement with you (for example, providing the Service you request, account administration, and payment processing through Stripe);
• Legitimate interests: processing necessary for our legitimate interests where not overridden by your rights (for example, securing the Service, debugging, preventing abuse, improving features, and internal analytics that do not require consent under applicable law);
• Consent: where we rely on consent (for example, certain cookies or marketing communications where required), you may withdraw consent at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before withdrawal;
• Legal obligation: processing necessary to comply with law.

You may contact {{email}} for more information about how we apply legal bases to specific processing.
